# LEGAL-007: BOARD RESOLUTIONS OF MEDSYNC HEALTH (2024)

## CERTIFICATE OF SECRETARY

The undersigned, Robert Foster, General Counsel and Secretary of **MedSync Health**, a Delaware corporation (the "Company"), hereby certifies that the following resolutions were duly adopted by the Board of Directors of the Company (the "Board") at a special meeting held on **June 30, 2024**, at the Company's headquarters located in **Boston, MA, USA**.

---

## I. MEETING DETAILS

**Date of Meeting:** June 30, 2024
**Location:** Corporate Headquarters, Boston, MA, USA
**Quorum:** A quorum was present and acting throughout the meeting.
**Attendees:** The following directors were present: Dr. Sarah Chen (CEO), Michael Rodriguez (CFO), Priya Patel (CTO), and other duly appointed directors (assumed).

---

## II. RESOLUTION CONCERNING SERIES D FUNDING APPROVAL

**WHEREAS**, the Company has successfully completed negotiations for a Series D financing round to secure capital for its continued growth, expansion into new markets (EMEA and APAC), and investment in its core product lines (MedSync Connect, MedSync Analytics, MedSync Patient Portal, and MedSync Compliance Suite); and

**WHEREAS**, the Board has reviewed and determined that the terms of the Series D Preferred Stock Purchase Agreement (the "Series D Agreement") and related documents are in the best interests of the Company and its stockholders; and

**WHEREAS**, the total capital to be raised in the Series D financing is **AED 551,250,000**, as detailed in the Company's Funding History (See FIN-001: Funding History Report);

**NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED**, that the Board hereby approves the Series D financing, including the issuance and sale of up to **AED 551,250,000** of Series D Preferred Stock, on the terms and conditions set forth in the Series D Agreement, substantially in the form presented to the Board; and

**BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED**, that the officers of the Company, including the CEO, Dr. Sarah Chen, and the CFO, Michael Rodriguez, are hereby authorized and directed to execute and deliver the Series D Agreement and all other necessary documents, and to take all actions necessary to consummate the Series D financing.

---

## III. RESOLUTION CONCERNING EXECUTIVE COMPENSATION APPROVAL

**WHEREAS**, the Compensation Committee of the Board has reviewed the performance of the Company's executive officers for the fiscal year 2024 and has proposed a revised executive compensation structure to ensure the Company remains competitive in attracting and retaining top-tier talent; and

**WHEREAS**, the proposed structure includes a base salary, performance-based bonuses, and equity incentives, consistent with the Company's compensation philosophy, which targets a C-Level average total compensation of approximately **AED 1,838,250**;

**NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED**, that the Board hereby approves the Executive Compensation Plan for the fiscal year 2024, including the base salaries, annual incentive plan targets, and long-term equity incentive grants for the executive officers, as presented to the Board; and

**BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED**, that the Compensation Committee is authorized to make minor adjustments to the approved compensation packages as necessary, provided such adjustments remain within the established budgetary and equity pool limits.

---

## IV. RESOLUTION CONCERNING STRATEGIC PARTNERSHIP APPROVAL

**WHEREAS**, the Company's management has identified a critical need to integrate advanced artificial intelligence capabilities into its MedSync Analytics and MedSync Compliance Suite products to maintain market leadership; and

**WHEREAS**, the management has negotiated a definitive agreement for a strategic partnership with **DeepMind Health** (a fictional entity representing a leading AI firm) for the co-development and exclusive licensing of a proprietary predictive analytics engine (the "AI Integration Partnership"); and

**WHEREAS**, the Board has reviewed the terms of the AI Integration Partnership and determined that it is strategically vital for the Company's long-term product roadmap and competitive positioning;

**NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED**, that the Board hereby approves the AI Integration Partnership with DeepMind Health, and the execution of the associated definitive agreements, substantially in the form presented to the Board; and

**BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED**, that the CTO, Priya Patel, and the CPO, David Kim, are authorized to allocate the necessary resources, including a budget of up to AED 15,000,000, to execute the terms of the AI Integration Partnership.

---

## V. GENERAL AUTHORIZATION AND COMPLIANCE

**BE IT RESOLVED**, that the officers of the Company are hereby authorized and directed to take all such further actions and to execute and deliver all such further agreements, certificates, instruments, and documents as may be necessary or desirable to carry out the intent and accomplish the purposes of the foregoing resolutions; and

**BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED**, that in connection with the Company's international operations, particularly in the EMEA region, the Board reaffirms its commitment to data privacy and security compliance. **See SEC-004 for GDPR compliance** documentation and audit reports.

---

